From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: signal the requested thread on PS4, not the process.

Archive 0930, with the thr_kill2 prototype corrected to the shim's
(pid_t, long, int). Without it tkill() returns ENOSYS on Prospero and
send_thread_signal() falls back to kill(pid, sig), so SuspendThread, APC
interrupts and thread kills reach an arbitrary thread. In GLDS10043 01.15
(2026-11-05) Half-Life's Quit and FNV's Exit to Desktop both crashed: the
server thread took the SIGUSR1 meant for a game thread, and its handler
faulted at NULL+0x1c in server_call_unlocked (stop_thread ->
send_thread_signal -> usr1 -> server_select).
---
diff --git a/server/ptrace.c b/server/ptrace.c
index 2e6d93b721..46fa1372a5 100644
--- a/server/ptrace.c
+++ b/server/ptrace.c
@@ -217,6 +217,17 @@ static int waitpid_thread( struct thread *thread, int signal )
     return (thread->unix_pid != -1);
 }
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+/* The console has no thr_kill2: the PS4 platform shim in the wineserver PRX
+ * (wine/ps5/pw_wine_threads.c) maps the id ntdll registered for each thread
+ * to its pthread_t and calls pthread_kill. Without this branch tkill() fails
+ * with ENOSYS and send_thread_signal() falls back to kill(pid), which lets the
+ * kernel pick any thread: on 2026-11-05 a game's SuspendThread at exit
+ * delivered SIGUSR1 to the server thread itself, whose handler then faulted
+ * at NULL+0x1c in server_call_unlocked (Half-Life and FNV quit crashes). */
+extern int thr_kill2( pid_t pid, long id, int sig );
+#endif
+
 /* send a signal to a specific thread */
 static inline int tkill( int tgid, int pid, int sig )
 {
@@ -224,6 +235,8 @@ static inline int tkill( int tgid, int pid, int sig )
     int ret = syscall( __NR_tgkill, tgid, pid, sig );
     if (ret < 0 && errno == ENOSYS) ret = syscall( __NR_tkill, pid, sig );
     return ret;
+#elif defined(__PROSPERO__)
+    return thr_kill2( tgid, pid, sig );
 #elif (defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined (__FreeBSD_kernel__)) && defined(HAVE_THR_KILL2)
     return thr_kill2( tgid, pid, sig );
 #else
